  "validation_domain": "33 guarded ARM target executions and actual-provider C++ replays. Outgoing queue0/1/5/6/7/12, separate incoming queue unchanged, six-message drain, control literals from both ELF objects, handshake clock-before-read/post/order and state-at-post, idle no-drain, strict heartbeat399/400/401 and expiry4999/5000/5001 including low32 carry, negative signed64 values and uint64 deadline wrap. CCL CLOCK_MONOTONIC captured through linker wrapper; no hardware operations. Host registered lazy singleton destruction verified after process exit main.",
  "limitations": [
    "Provisional void return; original ordinary declaration unresolved, deliver compiled declaration-pending, not ready.",
    "Independent borrowed portable state and typed queues, no original C1/C2 recovery, ARM layout, calling convention, hardware or binary interoperability claim.",
    "Native singleton preinitialized. Native allocation, constructor/Deletable registration, failure/unwind paths excluded. Host actual pinned CCL lazy Singleton/Deletable creation and automatic registered destruction executed with offline SPI/GPIO.",
    "ARM external boundaries are named controlled models: queue empty/readMIDI, memset/memcpy, signed divide, clock, post, packet constructor and singleton lookup. Oracle executes exact target instructions only; modeled queue data is valid frame domain. Constructor boundary models two clock reads; no claim to native provider closure execution.",
    "Host uses actual queue, SysexPacket, SPI post, CclResponseServices, packet clock gateway and pinned CCL Singleton. Hardware IO is captured at SpiServiceIO and InputPinIO; descriptor -1 with offline transfer accepted, receive data uniformly f8. Device update/erase/programming and incoming SPI response assembly not exercised.",
